@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Creating and Configuring Build Pipelines";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <h1 class="text-center text-primary">Creating and Configuring Build Pipelines</h1>
    <p class="lead text-center">Learn how to set up, configure, and manage build pipelines in Azure DevOps for automated CI/CD workflows.</p>
    <hr />

    <!-- Introduction -->
    <div class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="text-success">Introduction to Build Pipelines</h2>
        <p>
            Build pipelines in Azure DevOps help automate the process of compiling, testing, and packaging applications. They ensure consistent builds and reduce human intervention.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/build-pipeline-overview.jpg" alt="Build Pipeline Overview" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure DevOps Build Pipelines automate software compilation and testing.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Steps to Create a Build Pipeline -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-warning">Steps to Create a Build Pipeline</h2>
        <ol class="list-group list-group-numbered">
            <li class="list-group-item">Go to Azure DevOps and navigate to your project.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Click on "Pipelines" in the left-hand menu and select "New Pipeline".</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Choose your repository (Azure Repos, GitHub, or another source control system).</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Select a template or configure manually using YAML.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Define build steps, such as restoring dependencies, building code, and running tests.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Save and run the pipeline to test execution.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/build-pipeline-setup.jpg" alt="Build Pipeline Setup" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Setting up a build pipeline in Azure DevOps.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Configuring Build Pipelines -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-danger">Configuring Build Pipelines</h2>
        <p>
            Once the build pipeline is created, you can configure advanced options such as triggers, variables, and agent selection:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Triggers:</strong> Automate builds on code changes (continuous integration).</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Agent Pools:</strong> Define where builds run (Microsoft-hosted or self-hosted agents).</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Variables:</strong> Store environment-specific settings securely.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Artifacts:</strong> Manage output files for deployment.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/build-pipeline-configuration.jpg" alt="Build Pipeline Configuration" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Configuring build pipelines for better automation.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Best Practices -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-info">Best Practices for Build Pipelines</h2>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Use YAML Pipelines:</strong> YAML-based pipelines offer better version control.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Enable Continuous Integration:</strong> Automatically trigger builds on code commits.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Optimize Build Steps:</strong> Minimize build times with caching and parallel execution.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Monitor Build Logs:</strong> Regularly check logs for failures and inefficiencies.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Secure Secrets:</strong> Store API keys and credentials in Azure Key Vault.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/build-pipeline-best-practices.jpg" alt="Best Practices for Build Pipelines" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Following best practices improves efficiency and security.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Conclusion -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-secondary">Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Creating and configuring build pipelines in Azure DevOps is crucial for automating software delivery. By following best practices, teams can enhance productivity, reduce manual errors, and ensure consistent builds across environments.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/build-pipeline-conclusion.jpg" alt="Build Pipeline Summary" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Build pipelines streamline CI/CD workflows in modern development.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>